---
source: crates/cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: help
---
Command-line interface for rs-launch-blueprint.

Commands follow a noun-verb structure (for example `rslbp project list`).
Results are written to stdout; diagnostics, progress, prompts, and errors go to stderr.

Usage: rslbp [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  project      Manage project resources
  config       Inspect and edit layered configuration
  version      Print version and build metadata
  diagnostics  Inspect environment, configuration, and credential readiness
  completion   Print a shell completion script to stdout
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -V, --version
          Print version information and exit

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table:    Human-readable aligned table
          - json:     Machine-readable JSON document
          - markdown: GitHub-Flavored Markdown table
          - name:     Bare identifiers, one per line
          
          [env: RSLBP_OUTPUT]

      --json
          Shorthand for `--output json`

      --output-file <PATH>
          Write result output to a file path (`-` selects stdout)

      --no-clobber
          Refuse to overwrite an existing `--output-file` target

      --copy
          Copy rendered output to the system clipboard after writing primary output

      --no-pager
          Disable automatic terminal paging for table output

      --no-input
          Never prompt interactively; fail when required input or consent is missing

      --color <COLOR>
          Control terminal ANSI color emission

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Enable color automatically when the stream is a terminal
          - always: Force ANSI color sequences even when redirected
          - never:  Disable ANSI color sequences

      --no-color
          Disable terminal ANSI color emission (alias for `--color never`)

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase diagnostic log verbosity (`-v` info, `-vv` debug, `-vvv` trace)

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress progress indicators and non-essential stderr output

      --debug
          Enable trace-level diagnostics with source file, line, and thread metadata

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Explicit console diagnostic log level

          Possible values:
          - off:   Disable diagnostic logging
          - error: Errors only
          - warn:  Warnings and errors
          - info:  Operational info and above
          - debug: Debug diagnostics and above
          - trace: Trace diagnostics and above
          
          [env: RSLBP_LOG_LEVEL]

      --log-format <LOG_FORMAT>
          Console diagnostic log format

          Possible values:
          - auto:    Console when stderr is a terminal, JSON otherwise
          - console: Human-readable console lines
          - json:    Newline-delimited JSON events
          
          [env: RSLBP_LOG_FORMAT]

      --log-file[=<PATH>]
          Write rotating diagnostic logs to a file (omit value for default XDG state path)

      --config <PATH>
          Path to an explicit TOML configuration file (replaces layered discovery)
          
          [env: RSLBP_CONFIG]

      --token-file <PATH>
          Read API token from a file path (`-` reads from stdin)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
